meta {
  name: 03-SuspendUser
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{host}}/api/admin/users/{{suspendTargetUserId}}/suspend
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{jwt}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "reason": "Took inspection fee off-platform — confirmed via reporter screenshot in support ticket #4421. Agent admitted in WhatsApp screenshot to asking applicant to pay 25,000 NGN to personal Opay before showing the unit. Suspending pending review."
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

docs {
  # The serious action.

  Spec says reason has `minLength: 0` — same lie as reject and takedown.
  I'm sending a real one because that's what the persona doc demands.
  Will probe empty in Defensive-checks.

  Things I can't verify from the API alone:
  - Did the user's existing JWTs actually become invalid? Persona doc
    Story 4 says tokenVersion is bumped — but the response body isn't
    documented and I can't read tokenVersion from anywhere. I just have
    to TRUST the implementation.
  - Was a notification sent to the user? Not visible to me.
  - Was an audit log row written? No way to read it (no audit log
    endpoint exists).

  The whole "I did the right thing" feedback loop is implicit. For T&S
  that's the wrong default — sensitive actions should be loudly
  observable.
}
